eels very  luxurious apart from the gearshift this  number one symbolized outies high  standard since 1923 with the front  howdy entered the upper-middle-class  market the cars main selling point was  its modern technology front wheel drive  a box frame and a straight-6 engine with  an impressive 40 horsepower crystal says  the Audi front is also a feast for the  eyes with its shapely lines this  roadsters body was made by Glaser a  coach builder from Dresden Boston Jose  Glaser in Destin only a minority of Audi  front models received a closed car body  in the horse plant in neighboring Sekou  most LD front customers opted for the  open top versions produced by  convertible specialist Glaser in Dresden  they came with a choice of four or two  side windows  the dashboard gearshift is a typical  feature of early front wheel drives  Christophe Power says the letters u W in  the cars name stood for Olga Caravan  dava the back-to-front wanderer it  referred to the fact that the car  featured a wanderer engine that had been  turned around to drive wheels which were  now ahead of the engine unfortunately  the gearshift and transmission  diminished the driving pleasure  Christophe says that in 1933 the press  hailed the Audi fronts gearshift is one  of the most precise and smooth in a  front-wheel drive but he says that's not  true from today's perspective it rattles  and shudders especially in the first and  second gears the fourth and fifth aren't  bad provided you can find them it's not  so easy as this old gear shift has metre  long rods going into the gearbox in  front so it's not very precise and you  have to be careful with the reverse  there's no lock for it and changing into  the wrong gear can be costly only the  third and fourth gears are synchronized  but then again what trendsetter is  perfect christophe says Audion parked on  a new era with the audi front to this  day front-wheel drive is still one of  the car makers trademarks so the front  is always a hit at